{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345378",
      "title": "Using Functions as Values",
      "sourceHash": "42a81f5816dfeee75a99d5d4178fa37872dcb72eb2eb9cb9c340cdfddd700b6d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "And with that we're almost done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "for this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "but there are a couple of essential features that we'll use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "in this course and a couple of tricky features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 16.5,
          "en": "which I also wanna refresh here so that you know about these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.5,
          "end": 18.51,
          "en": "JavaScript concepts and features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.51,
          "end": 21.78,
          "en": "and you don't wonder about them when you encounter them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.78,
          "end": 24.03,
          "en": "later in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.03,
          "end": 27.45,
          "en": "The first JavaScript feature you should be aware of is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.45,
          "end": 31.803,
          "en": "that you can pass functions as values to other functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.97,
          "end": 35.1,
          "en": "For example, we could set a timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.1,
          "end": 38.04,
          "en": "with help of the built-in setTimeout function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.04,
          "end": 40.323,
          "en": "a function that is provided by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 44.91,
          "en": "Now setTimeout wants two input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.91,
          "end": 47.013,
          "en": "It accepts two parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 51.06,
          "en": "The first input value it wants is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.06,
          "end": 53.016,
          "en": "a function itself though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.016,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "a function that can be defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 59.04,
          "en": "with the function keyword or as an arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 61.68,
          "en": "Now, what's really important to understand here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 66.21,
          "en": "that what we're doing here is we're creating a new function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.21,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "an anonymous function here since it has no name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 71.73,
          "en": "but nonetheless, a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.73,
          "end": 75.42,
          "en": "and we could absolutely create that function manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.42,
          "end": 76.623,
          "en": "in a separate step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.18,
          "end": 81.81,
          "en": "It could be named handleTimeout or anything like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.81,
          "end": 84.507,
          "en": "and here we could console.log (\"Timed out\").",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.61,
          "end": 89.49,
          "en": "So this would now be a regular function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.49,
          "end": 92.13,
          "en": "and we could also alternatively define it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.13,
          "end": 93.81,
          "en": "as an arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 95.43299999999999,
          "en": "Could be named handleTimeout2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 99.53999999999999,
          "en": "and we store an arrow function in that constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.53999999999999,
          "end": 102.21000000000001,
          "en": "Because arrow functions never accept a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 103.17,
          "en": "in front of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.17,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "they always are created in an anonymous way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 110.13,
          "en": "but we can make them non-anonymous by then storing them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.13,
          "end": 113.283,
          "en": "in a constant or a variable that has a certain name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.9,
          "end": 118.83,
          "en": "and then here I could console.log (\"Timed out\") again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.83,
          "end": 120.33,
          "en": "anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "So here I'm creating a function with the function keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 126.09,
          "en": "or as an arrow function stored in a constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.09,
          "end": 128.79,
          "en": "And we can now also pass this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.79,
          "end": 131.37,
          "en": "or this constant that contains a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.37,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "as a value to set the timeout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 138.06,
          "en": "so as a value for this first parameter that wants a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.06,
          "end": 141.54,
          "en": "instead of defining the function right here in place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.54,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "which would be an alternative though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "Now what's really important to understand here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 150.32999999999998,
          "en": "when you're passing a function to another function though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.32999999999998,
          "end": 153.45,
          "en": "is that when you're not defining it here in place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.45,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "but instead you defined it in advance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 159.24,
          "en": "you pass it by just using its name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.24,
          "end": 161.25,
          "en": "so you don't add parentheses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.25,
          "end": 163.21,
          "en": "You omit those parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 166.53,
          "en": "because by just using the name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.53,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "you're passing the function as a value to this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 172.77,
          "en": "If you would add parentheses here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.77,
          "end": 175.742,
          "en": "you would instead make sure that this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.742,
          "end": 179.55,
          "en": "handleTimeout here gets executed immediately at the point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.55,
          "end": 182.82,
          "en": "of time when this timer is set, in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.82,
          "end": 187.08,
          "en": "and therefore it would be the return value of that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.08,
          "end": 190.77,
          "en": "If it would return any value, which this one does not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.77,
          "end": 194.46,
          "en": "that would be passed as a value for this first argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 198.12,
          "en": "this first parameter, to setTimeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.12,
          "end": 200.94,
          "en": "And that, of course, would be the wrong thing to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 204.12,
          "en": "because here I don't wanna pass the return value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.12,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "of that function to setTimeout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 208.473,
          "en": "but instead the function itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.46,
          "end": 213.81,
          "en": "so that internally setTimeout can execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.81,
          "end": 216.27,
          "en": "at some point in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.27,
          "end": 218.97,
          "en": "And that's why you must omit the parentheses here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.97,
          "end": 221.7,
          "en": "so that you don't execute this function right away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.7,
          "end": 225.573,
          "en": "and you instead pass the function as a value to set.Timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.59,
          "end": 229.14,
          "en": "Well, and then here, set.Timeout takes a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.14,
          "end": 232.41,
          "en": "second argument as well, which is now not a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.41,
          "end": 235.14,
          "en": "but instead a number which defines the number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.14,
          "end": 237.48,
          "en": "of milliseconds JavaScript should wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.48,
          "end": 239.91,
          "en": "until it executes this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.91,
          "end": 242.853,
          "en": "which you passed as a first argument to set.Timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.35,
          "end": 247.1,
          "en": "And I can, of course, also do that with handleTimeout2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 250.11,
          "en": "Now, just to be clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 250.11,
          "end": 254.04,
          "en": "you can always create an anonymous function instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.04,
          "end": 256.38,
          "en": "of defining a function in advance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.38,
          "end": 258.45,
          "en": "and then you could, of course, also add any code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 258.45,
          "end": 260.313,
          "en": "you want to execute to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 261.75,
          "end": 264.18,
          "en": "But when you define such an anonymous function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.18,
          "end": 266.64,
          "en": "you're also not executing it yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.64,
          "end": 268.83,
          "en": "Instead, you're also just defining it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.83,
          "end": 272.94,
          "en": "and you're passing that defined function to set.Timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.94,
          "end": 276.39,
          "en": "So you're in the end doing the same as you're doing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 276.39,
          "end": 278.15999999999997,
          "en": "by defining it in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.15999999999997,
          "end": 280.98,
          "en": "and passing a handler to that function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 280.98,
          "end": 283.59000000000003,
          "en": "the name of the function to setTimeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.59000000000003,
          "end": 285.51,
          "en": "You're essentially doing the same here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 285.51,
          "end": 288.84000000000003,
          "en": "when defining the function in the place where it's needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.84000000000003,
          "end": 291.06,
          "en": "You're still only defining it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.06,
          "end": 293.343,
          "en": "You're not executing it immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 298.23,
          "en": "Well, and therefore here, if you save that and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.23,
          "end": 299.76,
          "en": "you'll see nothing initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 299.76,
          "end": 302.25,
          "en": "but then once these timers expire,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.25,
          "end": 305.67,
          "en": "you will see the different messages they output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 305.67,
          "end": 309.21,
          "en": "Now knowing that you can pass functions as values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 309.21,
          "end": 312.96,
          "en": "to other functions is an important first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 312.96,
          "end": 315.9,
          "en": "but you should not think that this is only possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 315.9,
          "end": 319.74,
          "en": "for built-in functions like set.Timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 319.74,
          "end": 322.36,
          "en": "Instead, you can also build your own function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 323.548,
          "end": 328.17,
          "en": "like greeter, for example, which accepts a greet function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 328.17,
          "end": 331.71,
          "en": "parameter so a regular parameter in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 331.71,
          "end": 336.71,
          "en": "but a parameter which expects to get a function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 337.77,
          "end": 339.6,
          "en": "And then inside of greeter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 339.6,
          "end": 342.93,
          "en": "we could execute greet function like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 342.93,
          "end": 346.863,
          "en": "so calling it as a function by adding these parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.97,
          "end": 351.48,
          "en": "and now we could call greeter like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.48,
          "end": 354.03,
          "en": "and pass a function to greeter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.03,
          "end": 356.85,
          "en": "like, for example, here an arrow function where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.85,
          "end": 358.287,
          "en": "I console.log('Hi').",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 360.6,
          "end": 363.13,
          "en": "If I do that and save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 364.41,
          "end": 367.5,
          "en": "and reload this page and open this console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 367.5,
          "end": 369.81,
          "en": "you will see Hi here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 369.81,
          "end": 372.18,
          "en": "and this Hi is, of course, coming from this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 372.18,
          "end": 374.46,
          "en": "console.log message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 374.46,
          "end": 377.97,
          "en": "so this function here is getting executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 377.97,
          "end": 380.97,
          "en": "because we're passing it as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 380.97,
          "end": 385.56,
          "en": "for this greetFn parameter to the greeter function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 385.56,
          "end": 388.14,
          "en": "and inside of that greeter function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 388.14,
          "end": 391.44,
          "en": "I'm then executing this greetFn parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 391.44,
          "end": 394.68,
          "en": "so the value that's received on that parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 394.68,
          "end": 396.84000000000003,
          "en": "which is this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 396.84000000000003,
          "end": 401.84000000000003,
          "en": "So this function down here is passed as a value to greetFn,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 404.7,
          "end": 407.79,
          "en": "and then greetFn is executed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 407.79,
          "end": 411.45,
          "en": "Therefore, indirectly, this function is getting executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 411.45,
          "end": 416.01,
          "en": "there because this function down there at the bottom is the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 416.01,
          "end": 418.593,
          "en": "value received here on greetFn.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 419.43,
          "end": 421.17,
          "en": "And I just wanted to mention this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
